    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="validation-records" tabindex="-1">Validation records <a class="header-anchor" href="#validation-records" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Validation records&quot;">\u200B</a></h1><h2 id="_0-5-1-gray-connection-retry" tabindex="-1">0.5.1: gray connection retry <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-5-1-gray-connection-retry" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.5.1: gray connection retry&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Recorded 2026-11-18 on Windows/Node 24.19.0. The sidebar regression exercises emitted connection actions: a gray configured agent retries setup, including historical MCP and current hook-only observations; a green observed agent disconnects; an unconfigured agent connects. Keyboard retry, accessible labels and tooltip guidance are included in the <strong>32-test UI suite</strong>. Release qualification also covers canonical skill consistency, TypeScript, backend tests and the complete documentation build.</p><p>The final VSIX is qualified in isolated VS Code and IBM Bob profiles, with package/runtime version agreement and its published SHA-256 checked. Package reports are retained in the repository: <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/main/artifacts/host-release-051-vscode.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">VS Code</a>, <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/main/artifacts/host-release-051-bob.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">IBM Bob</a> and <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/main/artifacts/release-0.5.1-package.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">package inspection</a>. Live editor installations are unchanged.</p><p>This patch corrects the footer action. It does not establish why a native client has sent no traffic, approve hooks, or force native MCP reload. Native hook trust approval, authenticated conversations, remote/multi-root workspaces, other operating systems and large-project performance remain outside this qualification.</p><h2 id="_0-5-0-governed-knowledge-project-releases-and-native-recovery" tabindex="-1">0.5.0: governed knowledge, project releases and native recovery <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-5-0-governed-knowledge-project-releases-and-native-recovery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.5.0: governed knowledge, project releases and native recovery&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>The final implementation passed <strong>89 backend tests</strong>, <strong>32 UI tests</strong>, typechecking, canonical/workspace skill drift checks and all three skill validators. This release adds its own notes page to the complete documentation build. Catalog checks cover immutable definitions, human-only approval, source/test freshness and completion accounting, resumable baseline migration and paginated project export. Nine real-Git tests cover global commit membership, version/changelog edits, local commit/tag operations, remote tag-only publication, hooks, CRLF, concurrency, interrupted-result recovery, shallow history and side-branch tags. Native/headless service contracts and UI review/apply/publish paths are exercised.</p><p>The 0.5.0 VSIX is rebuilt with matching package/lock/runtime metadata. Release qualification runs both isolated editor hosts against the extracted package and verifies its SHA-256 against the attached checksum. Reports: <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-release-050-vscode.json">VS Code</a>, <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-release-050-bob.json">IBM Bob</a>, and <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-reload.json">automatic restart</a>. The scope of native trust/chat coverage is described below.</p><p>Recorded 2026-11-18 on Windows/Node 24. Regression tests cover a previously connected MCP client whose first mutation spans delayed workspace restart, retained project identity, no mutation replay after a lost response, tool-contract mismatch, current versus historical traffic, and persisted restart prompt/automatic/never behavior including declined/failed restart and identical-config reinstall. UI coverage checks that historical traffic alone stays grey.</p><p>The installed Codex <code>codex_vscode/0.169.0-alpha.11.1</code> app-server passed MCP inventory/calls, delayed service restart and resuming a persisted disposable thread from a fresh native process, using an isolated home and offline provider. No model turn, credentials or user chat was used. This does not qualify the Codex chat webview or all older thread formats. The test remains reproducible through <code>scripts/codex-resume-smoke.ts</code>.</p><p>VS Code 1.145.3 passed an actual automatic first-setup Extension Host restart in an isolated profile, then verified installed hook execution/current observation and unchanged reconnect without a restart loop. The native-agent fixture was not activated; hook trust approval remains untested and client-owned. Reports are <code>artifacts/codex-resume.json</code> and <code>artifacts/host-reload.json</code>; see <a href="./DEVELOPMENT.html#qualify-native-reconnection-and-setup-reload">development</a> for commands.</p><h2 id="_0-4-0-isolated-reference-codebases" tabindex="-1">0.4.0: isolated reference codebases <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-4-0-isolated-reference-codebases" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.4.0: isolated reference codebases&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Recorded 2026-11-17 on Windows/Node 24: reference tests cover concurrent same-path/same-symbol repositories, separation from current project memory and records, restart persistence, saved-file freshness, scoped context budgets, impact/path/search/flow, invalid roots and aliases, safe detachment, and Windows storage paths over 260 characters. Native and standalone MCP, CLI registration/selection and editor source-resolution checks exercise the advertised contracts. UI checks cover reference selection, source/trace scope, stale response rejection and narrow layouts. Portable skill validation, workspace/bundle drift, typecheck, <strong>63 backend tests</strong>, <strong>29 UI tests</strong> and the complete <strong>23-page</strong> documentation build pass.</p><p>The extracted 0.4.0 VSIX passes the full scenario in <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-reference-package-vscode.json">VS Code 1.145.3</a> and <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-reference-package-bob.json">IBM Bob, VS Code API 1.126.0</a>. The new host step verifies reference architecture and source flow while a same-path current-project buffer is unsaved, then detaches and confirms the reference&#39;s bytes and directory contents are unchanged. This exposed and fixed SQLite&#39;s Windows path limit in long editor storage directories. MCP transport tests also exposed and fixed a non-object root input schema during implementation.</p><p>The release includes matching VSIX/checksum assets and a full documentation build. Package runtime and portable skill bytes match those exercised in both hosts. Live editor installations are unchanged. These checks do not qualify authenticated model conversations, remote/multi-root workspaces, other operating systems or large-repository performance. Reference search remains lexical and reference freshness is checked on demand.</p><h2 id="_0-3-1-patch-release-packaging" tabindex="-1">0.3.1: patch release packaging <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-3-1-patch-release-packaging" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.3.1: patch release packaging&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Recorded 2026-11-16 on Windows/Node 24.19.0: <code>npm run check</code> passes skill bundle consistency, TypeScript checking, production builds, <strong>58 backend tests</strong> and <strong>28 UI tests</strong>. The complete documentation build checks all <strong>22 pages</strong> and generated page/asset links. Documentation source links and the live release-page check now use the package version.</p><p>The extracted 0.3.1 VSIX passes the full packaged scenario in <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-release-031-vscode.json">VS Code 1.145.3</a> and <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-release-031-bob.json">IBM Bob, VS Code API 1.126.0</a>. The <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/release-0.3.1-package.json">package inspection</a> checks the version, release notes, exact runtime bundles and all four canonical skill resources, and excludes development/private files. The final package includes this validation record; its runtime and skill bytes match those exercised in both hosts. Its matching SHA-256 is supplied with the GitHub release.</p><p><code>npm run release:verify</code> checks the public tag and downloaded assets, HTTPS Pages configuration, preserved orphan branch history, complete documentation manifest and current release page. Hosted documentation Actions are currently prevented from starting by the GitHub account&#39;s billing lock; the generated site can still be deployed through the existing branch-based Pages configuration. No account or billing settings are changed. Existing platform and authenticated-agent qualification limits below remain applicable.</p><h2 id="_0-3-0-release-publication-and-visual-exploration" tabindex="-1">0.3.0: release publication and visual exploration <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-3-0-release-publication-and-visual-exploration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.3.0: release publication and visual exploration&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>The publication follow-up updates the installation/upgrade links and release notes and builds the full documentation with VitePress, local search and Mermaid diagrams. All 21 Markdown pages (guides, release notes, skills/references, README and changelog) are staged from canonical sources. The build checks generated page and asset links; GitHub Pages publishes the static output from an orphan <code>gh-pages</code> branch. Documentation tooling is excluded from the VSIX.</p><p>Architecture now combines a subsystem map, bounded file shortcuts and symbol neighborhoods with coordinated selection, breadcrumbs/Back, relationship/direction filters, source inspection and a directional matrix. Code map adds a step explorer/inspector, direct-neighbor focus, filters, zoom/pan/fit and retained keyboard/viewport state. New browser regressions exercise those workflows alongside existing empty/error, narrow, live-theme, Panel and source/export checks. <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/architecture-explorer.png">Architecture preview</a> \xB7 <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/code-map-explorer.png">Code map preview</a>.</p><p>Recorded 2026-11-16 on Windows/Node 24.19.0: the full check passes <strong>58 backend tests</strong> (including real local embeddings) and <strong>28 UI tests</strong>, skill bundle consistency, TypeScript checking and production bundles. Browser inspection of the generated documentation verifies navigation, local full-text search, Mermaid rendering and a 390-pixel mobile viewport. The generated page/asset link check covers all <strong>21 pages</strong>.</p><p>The extracted release package passes the full host scenario in <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-release-030-vscode.json">VS Code 1.145.3</a> and <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-release-030-bob.json">IBM Bob, VS Code API 1.126.0</a>. The <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/release-0.3.0-package.json">final package inspection</a> verifies byte-identical validated runtime bundles and all four canonical skill resources, the version and release notes, and exclusion of source/tests, private client configuration, source maps, documentation tooling and CI files. The package is rebuilt to include the final documentation; its runtime and skill bytes match those exercised by the host scenarios. The matching SHA-256 accompanies the release asset.</p><p><code>npm run release:verify</code> independently checks the published tag, downloaded VSIX/checksum bytes, GitHub Pages branch/root/HTTPS settings, orphan branch history, the complete live page manifest and key live guides. Earlier implementation measurements below remain historical evidence. Authenticated native-model conversations and the remote/platform/scale limits below remain unqualified.</p><h2 id="_0-3-0-code-intelligence-and-portable-execution-implementation-history" tabindex="-1">0.3.0: code intelligence and portable execution (implementation history) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-3-0-code-intelligence-and-portable-execution-implementation-history" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.3.0: code intelligence and portable execution (implementation history)&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>The agent-guidance follow-up synchronizes both canonical skills and their references across all four workspace adapters (16 resources), adds repository entry instructions and shares native/headless MCP guidance, brief arrays and lifecycle reminders. <strong>58 backend tests</strong> and <strong>23 UI tests</strong> pass; both skills pass the skill-creator validator and workspace/bundle drift checks pass. The 15 portability checks exercise real MCP initialization with exact shared instructions, brief consistency, all three reminder events for Codex/Claude/Bob, generic operation, byte-preserving skill-only sync, cross-client ownership-conflict preflight and CLI drift detection. This exposed and fixed a dropped PostCompact reminder. The refreshed local package is checked against the validated runtime bundles and canonical skills in <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/agent-guidance-package-inspection.json">package inspection</a>; its SHA-256 is refreshed. The editor-host reports below cover the earlier 0.3.0 package, before this guidance follow-up; authenticated model behavior remains unqualified.</p><p>Recorded 2026-11-16 on Windows/Node 24.19.0: <code>npm run check</code> passes skill-bundle drift checking, TypeScript checking, all production bundles, <strong>56 backend tests</strong> and <strong>23 Playwright tests</strong>, including the real local embedding test. Both canonical skills pass the skill-creator frontmatter/scaffold validator. New coverage includes stable declarations/aliases/tsconfig paths/inheritance, documents/tests/configuration, source edits/rename/deletion, bounded context and source-record impact, inferred contract paths, Graphify validation/provenance/replacement/invalidation, Python shadowing/duplicate declarations, concurrent freshness, schema 3-to-4 migration, ignored-parent workspaces, canonical resources, generic/no-hook installation, all native adapters, CLI persistence, stdio EOF cleanup and attachment to a live service.</p><p>Architecture UI checks cover queries, source/record navigation, refresh, empty/building/failed/partial states, light/dark styling and a 320-pixel view. Screenshots were visually inspected: <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/architecture-dark.png">dark</a> and <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/architecture-light-320.png">light/narrow</a>. Existing requests/history/flow/relationships/theme/Panel tests remain passing.</p><p><code>npm run evaluate:codebase</code> produces <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/codebase-evaluation.json">the nine-file checkout evaluation</a>. Both target definitions rank first with full expected-file recall; all three expected call edges, the inferred send/handler path, the linked decision and removal of obsolete edges pass. Response byte budgets are enforced; the artifact records actual indexing/query/cached-brief latency. These are deterministic regression measurements, not large-repository or model-following claims. A separate local CLI check indexed Contextory itself (102 selected files, over 2,500 symbols/11,000 edges) and exposed external/dynamic gaps explicitly. Review of that result led to exact-definition seeds, callable-member/record priority and reserved relationship space.</p><p>The development extension passed the full VS Code 1.145.3 scenario, including the Architecture workbench, context/path tools and generic MCP/skill export: <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-codebase-vscode.json">host report</a>. The extracted 0.3.0 package passed the same scenario in <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-codebase-package-vscode.json">VS Code 1.145.3</a> and <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-codebase-package-bob.json">IBM Bob, VS Code API 1.126.0</a>. Package inspection confirms both workers, both Python parsers, the CLI and all canonical skill/reference resources; development sources, tests, source maps and private client configuration are excluded. The VSIX and SHA-256 are local artifacts; no release was published. The default host launcher encountered an existing broken <code>.contextory-local/debug-runtime</code> junction pointing to the former project location; the check used the already cached pinned VS Code executable directly and preserved the junction.</p><p>Headless operation and generic MCP were exercised through actual processes and MCP SDK transport without editor clients/hooks. Native authenticated model conversations, cloud/remote execution, other operating systems, nested build-project semantics and large-monorepo performance remain unqualified. Static links and test references do not establish runtime delivery or execution coverage. Graphify is an optional import format, with source hashes and supplied provenance; no Graphify runtime or source is bundled.</p><h2 id="_0-2-6-automatic-agent-discovery-and-early-mcp-startup" tabindex="-1">0.2.6: automatic agent discovery and early MCP startup <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-2-6-automatic-agent-discovery-and-early-mcp-startup" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.2.6: automatic agent discovery and early MCP startup&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Recorded 2026-11-13: production builds, TypeScript checking, <strong>41 backend tests</strong> and <strong>20 Playwright tests</strong> pass, including real local embeddings. Detection cases cover exact case-insensitive extension IDs, inactive extensions, the Bob host, all detected providers, paused automation, explicit workspace disconnects and the retained startup modes. A real stdio client discovers all 19 tools before the workspace service exists, with exact catalog equality to the canonical schemas; a pending mutation succeeds once after the service starts without reconnecting the native client. Existing descriptor-rotation and role-isolation checks still pass.</p><p>Visual review of the production webview covers the new footer switch in the <strong>320\xD7800</strong> sidebar, <strong>760\xD7260</strong> Panel, and wide light-theme Panel. The switch remains visible with overflowing request lists and alongside the compact agent controls. UI checks exercise pause/resume across navigation, refresh, Panel/sidebar resizing and keyboard input, without disconnecting an existing provider.</p><p>The development extension passed the full <strong>VS Code 1.145.3</strong> host scenario: all detected inactive Codex/Claude fixtures were configured before opening Contextory or starting a session, and pausing/resuming preserved existing configuration bytes. The fixtures deliberately fail if activated. These checks exercise discovery and configuration, not authenticated native chat or client-owned trust/reload. Report: <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-discovery-dev-vscode.json">development VS Code</a>.</p><p>The <strong>extracted 0.2.6 VSIX passed</strong> the full scenario in <strong>VS Code 1.145.3</strong> and <strong>IBM Bob (VS Code API 1.126.0)</strong>. VS Code prepared both inactive agent fixtures and did not automatically create Bob configuration; the Bob host additionally prepared its own MCP/hooks. A separate paused cold-start run created no provider configuration until resumed, then discovered both installed fixtures. All runs used disposable workspaces and isolated profiles. Reports: <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-discovery-vscode.json">VS Code</a>, <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-discovery-bob.json">Bob</a>, <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-discovery-paused-vscode.json">paused startup</a>.</p><h2 id="_0-2-5-horizontal-panel-and-startup-preparation" tabindex="-1">0.2.5: horizontal Panel and startup preparation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-2-5-horizontal-panel-and-startup-preparation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.2.5: horizontal Panel and startup preparation&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Recorded 2026-11-13: production builds, TypeScript checking, <strong>38 backend tests</strong> and <strong>19 Playwright tests</strong> pass. Four new startup policy cases cover actual MCP/hook timestamps, later manual choices, local/global fallback, explicit defaults, <code>none</code> and preserved disconnects. The service notifies the editor of native MCP discovery/read activity so agent memory and connection indicators refresh without waiting for a record mutation.</p><p>The production webview was visually reviewed with fixture records at <strong>760\xD7260</strong>, <strong>1280\xD7420</strong> and <strong>1920\xD7360</strong>, plus the <strong>320\xD7800</strong> sidebar, light and high-contrast themes. Screenshots cover Overview, Requests, fully loaded History and source flow. Follow-up changes tightened recent activity and spec spacing and kept a useful diagram area in very short panels. Geometry checks cover pinned footers, no page-width overflow, scrollable long lists and a readable selected-spec inspector. Resize tests preserve drafts, the detail tab and expanded milestones. Workspace names remain visible on every tab and standalone view; long names truncate without interpreting markup.</p><p>The host smoke scenario also checks that a configured startup provider&#39;s project MCP/hooks and service descriptor exist before the view opens or a native session starts. This prepares the bridge; it does not emulate an authenticated native session or bypass client trust/reload.</p><p>The <strong>extracted 0.2.5 VSIX passed</strong> the full host scenario in <strong>VS Code 1.145.3</strong> and <strong>IBM Bob (VS Code API 1.126.0)</strong>, including startup preparation before opening the view. Both runs used disposable workspaces and isolated editor profiles. Local reports: <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-panel-vscode.json">VS Code</a> and <a href="/Contextory/artifacts/host-panel-bob.json">Bob</a>.</p><h2 id="_0-2-4-native-model-and-usage-records" tabindex="-1">0.2.4: native model and usage records <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-2-4-native-model-and-usage-records" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.2.4: native model and usage records&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Recorded 2026-11-12 on <code>feat/agent-usage-records</code>: TypeScript checking, all production bundles, <strong>34 backend tests</strong> and <strong>11 Playwright UI tests</strong> pass, including the real local embedding check. Seven new backend cases cover metadata-only normalization, identical/retried attempts, null versus zero counters, exact session/lease attribution, ambiguity/expiry/subagents, model changes, report filtering, additive migration, restart persistence and pagination. The actual built hook launcher forwards token fixtures over authenticated loopback RPC without transcript/prompt/error retention or model-visible output. The actual MCP transport advertises all 19 tools. UI coverage includes the Usage tab, refresh, missing counters and escaping native model names.</p><p>These are protocol fixtures and automated checks; live authenticated <code>PostModelRequest</code> delivery and provider-native trust/reload remain user qualification steps. Codex token counters require a native version exposing that hook. Claude model-switch hooks require 2.1.251+; Claude/Bob standard lifecycle hooks do not supply general token totals. Usage observations are local metadata, not billing or quota. Packages exclude project-specific agent configuration and skills.</p><h2 id="_0-2-3-qualification-record" tabindex="-1">0.2.3 qualification record <a class="header-anchor" href="#_0-2-3-qualification-record" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.2.3 qualification record&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Recorded 2026-11-12 on Windows with Node 24.19.0. Branch: <code>redesign/native-agent-foundation</code>.</p><h2 id="automated-checks" tabindex="-1">Automated checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#automated-checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Automated checks&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Validation passes TypeScript checking, all six production bundles plus the packaged Python AST parser, <strong>27 core/analysis/integration tests</strong>, and <strong>10 Playwright UI tests</strong>. The real local embedding test ran and passed; it was not skipped in this validation. The MCP workflow and registration checks use the renamed <code>contextory_</code> tools, managed skills and hook launcher.</p><p>Coverage includes idempotency/revisions, competing provider leases and expiry, dependency cycles, current independent evidence, durable explanations, source/contract changes, later failed checks, cancellation, historical records, late text chunks, missing-model fallback, stale source/vectors, graph recursion/diamonds/limits/early returns/finally, imports and unsaved overlays. Python tests exercise source-only parsing without executing a module, imports/aliases/methods, branches/loops/finally, recursion, parameter-dispatch boundaries, incoming calls, callee expansion and stale snapshots. A full-history test pages more than 125 events with descendant filtering and hierarchy links.</p><p>Real MCP SDK stdio coverage includes all exposed management/search/flow/history tools and a complete agent workflow: create request/milestone/spec, claim a lease, run an independent check, submit an outcome, execute its returned completion action and confirm completed spec/milestone/request records. Adding planned work and reopening a spec reopen parents. Request reports exclude unrelated work and include criteria, changes and test results. Other integration checks cover all three hook output formats, role isolation, authenticated loopback requests, descriptor rotation, job restart recovery, owned registration/disconnect, configuration conflicts and junction rejection.</p><p>UI checks exercise all open requests, three recent activities, pinned footer connection controls and determinate request progress bars, inline spec expansion, new requests, explanation tabs, evidence origins, keyboard tabs, escaping, descendant filtering, 85-event history pagination, linked navigation and request-specific report messages. Diagram tests cover source navigation, expansion/exports and the separate flow surface. Both 320/860-pixel layouts pass. Fixture screenshots were inspected: <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/companion-sidebar.png" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">sidebar</a>, <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/request-details.png" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">request details</a>, <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/request-history.png" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">history</a>, <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/source-flow.png" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">source flow</a>, <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/relationships.png" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">relationships</a>. These are preview fixtures, not evidence of a native model conversation.</p><p>Footer pinning is checked while scrolling long content and filtering to a short list at 320/860 pixels. Relationship coverage verifies readable record titles/IDs, descriptions, rationale, source navigation, and returning to the owning spec decision tab. Backend checks verify summary/source projections, deduplicated edges and bounded endpoints. History pagination preserves its scroll position.</p><p>Live theme regression checks simulate the CSS variables and body classes that VS Code supplies, switch through dark/light/custom and both high-contrast modes, and confirm that the same request elements and draft text survive. They cover sidebar/editor backgrounds, foregrounds, input fields, button color pairs, the inline brand icon, focus rings, progress colors, graph fills/text/edges, relationship cards and contrast borders. Preview screenshots were visually inspected: <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/themes.png" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">theme variants</a> and <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/contextory-brand.png" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">icon at sidebar sizes</a>. Production uses the editor&#39;s injected tokens; the sample theme palettes are excluded from the package.</p><h2 id="actual-editor-hosts-and-packaging" tabindex="-1">Actual editor hosts and packaging <a class="header-anchor" href="#actual-editor-hosts-and-packaging" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Actual editor hosts and packaging&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>The isolated host test passes in:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Host</th><th>Version</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visual Studio Code</td><td>1.145.3</td><td>Activation, commands, sidebar, external service, workflow mutation, provider configurations, TS worker, Python AST, remembered cursor, no extra sidebar trace tab, overlays, a dedicated relationship workbench with request/file summaries, request report and ledger</td></tr><tr><td>IBM Bob</td><td>VS Code API 1.126.0; installed Bob 2.2.1</td><td>Same host test using the supplied <code>IBM Bob.exe</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>The test uses a unique disposable workspace and user/extensions directories. It does not edit the user&#39;s real provider/global settings. Both hosts also passed against the extracted VSIX through <code>-ExtensionPath</code>; the reports identify that packaged extension path. Raw reports: <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/host-vscode.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">VS Code</a>, <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/host-bob.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Bob</a>.</p><p><code>npm run package:vsix</code> produces <code>artifacts/contextory-workspace-0.2.3.vsix</code>, approximately <strong>1.9 MB compressed</strong>. Its identity is <code>contextory-local.contextory-workspace</code>. It includes the monochrome activity-bar mark and color extension icon, service, TypeScript worker, Python AST script, MCP/hook launchers, webview/styles, architecture/plan/template/validation docs, optional model-preparation script and dependency notices. It excludes source maps, tests, models, developer runtimes, previous chat/router outputs and screenshots. Python analysis uses the installed Python 3.10+ executable rather than bundling an interpreter.</p><h2 id="measured-fixture" tabindex="-1">Measured fixture <a class="header-anchor" href="#measured-fixture" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Measured fixture&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>The retained 0.2.1 engine benchmark uses 200 source files (100 TS and 100 Python, approximately 2,200 functions per language), 2,000 project records, five call hops and fresh hook processes. Hardware: Intel Core Ultra 9 285H, 16 logical CPUs, 31.4 GiB RAM. Raw data: <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/blob/v0.2.3/artifacts/benchmark.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">benchmark.json</a>.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th style="text-align:right;">Median</th><th style="text-align:right;">p95</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Health RPC, 30 samples</td><td style="text-align:right;">15.94 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">19.17 ms</td></tr><tr><td>Lexical search, 20 samples</td><td style="text-align:right;">15.95 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">20.01 ms</td></tr><tr><td>Warm TS flow, 10 samples</td><td style="text-align:right;">66.28 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">72.16 ms</td></tr><tr><td>Repeated Python flow, 10 samples</td><td style="text-align:right;">230.46 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">260.55 ms</td></tr><tr><td>Health RPC during TS analysis, 20</td><td style="text-align:right;">21.98 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">25.09 ms</td></tr><tr><td>Health RPC during Python analysis, 20</td><td style="text-align:right;">19.48 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">21.32 ms</td></tr><tr><td>Complete dashboard, 2,000 records, 10</td><td style="text-align:right;">17.25 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">18.60 ms</td></tr><tr><td>Hook process, 8 samples</td><td style="text-align:right;">128.81 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">152.07 ms</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Single observations: service setup 41.34 ms (in-process, excludes external process startup), first TS worker/flow 472.46 ms, first Python flow 250.56 ms, source index 1,019.90 ms, seeding records/revisions 508.04 ms. Harness + service + active compiler worker RSS was 253.5 MiB; this does <strong>not</strong> measure idle extension overhead, isolate service RSS or include a separate peak Python-process measurement. Repeated Python queries include a fresh parser process and a bounded workspace scan. The earlier proposed 100 ms hook target was not met at p95; the current advisory RPC deadline is 450 ms plus native-client process overhead. No claim is made that all original performance targets passed.</p><p>The optional model/runtime occupies about 486 MiB on this Windows installation. Cold model integration testing takes roughly 13\u201316 seconds including load, several embeddings and test cleanup. Warm model latency, multilingual/code retrieval quality and large indexes have not been qualified. The small semantic fixture retrieves a credential-renewal record ahead of unrelated color-palette text and rejects an obsolete vector after revision.</p><h2 id="qualification-limits" tabindex="-1">Qualification limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#qualification-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Qualification limits&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>No authenticated model conversation was driven through the actual Codex, Claude Code or Bob native chat extension during this validation. Standard MCP clients now demonstrate a complete spec workflow through the actual stdio bridge; generated configurations, hook launchers and editor hosts are also tested. Provider-native hook trust/reload and a model following the completion instructions still need a live native-chat run in each client before claiming full provider qualification.</p><p>Also unqualified: WSL/SSH/containers, multi-root folders, other operating systems, universal language/framework flow extraction, runtime instrumentation, sustained idle CPU, and 10k/100k-file or 100k-record workloads. Static source diagrams show possible bounded paths, not exhaustive runtime behavior. Search, optional vectors and explicit relationships assist navigation; they do not prove complete impact or correctness.</p>', 67)
